# Z.AI GLM-4.5-Flash — findings by Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B A12B

> Source: Z.AI (glm-4.5-flash)
> Date: 2026-10-25 (UTC)
> Overview and scoring methodology: ../../model-comparison.md
> Cross-model signed log: ../../model-findings.md

## Model card

- **Name:** GLM-4.5-Flash
- **Short description:** Z.AI's free flash variant in the GLM-4.5 MoE series, positioned for strong reasoning, coding, and agent workloads; part of GLM-4.5 family (GLM-4.5: 355B total/32B active; GLM-4.5-Air: 106B total/12B active).
- **Provider / access:** Z.AI API (`glm-4.5-flash`), Hugging Face (zai-org). MIT license.
- **Release / knowledge:** GLM-4.5 released July 28, 2025 (AA); docs indicate newer GLM-4.6/GLM-5.3 releases exist.
- **IDs:** `glm-4.5-flash` (Z.AI API).
- **Context window:** 128K tokens (official docs); AA lists 130k tokens (minor discrepancy); max output 96K tokens.
- **Modalities:** Text in; text out. Thinking Mode / Non-Thinking Mode hybrid reasoning. Function calling, web search, tool streaming, context caching, structured output supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-25):** Listed as "Free" tier in official docs; AA lists no pricing data for GLM-4.5 (deprecated).
- **Architecture:** MoE (Mixture-of-Experts); Flash variant parameter count not separately published (family: 355B/32B for GLM-4.5, 106B/12B for GLM-4.5-Air). License MIT.

### Raw benchmarks found

- Artificial Intelligence Index: **13** (estimated; #86/121 open-weights, median 19 — below average); GLM-4.5 marked **deprecated** by AA, superseded by GLM-4.6.
- benchgap (3 measured / 20 estimated, data 2026-10-24): GPQA Diamond 79.9% estimated ±1.7 pp; SWE-bench Verified 76.3% estimated ±4.4 pp; AA Coding Index 59.6% estimated ±9.0 pp; Vals GPQA Diamond 72.2% measured; Vals LiveCodeBench 67.4% measured; Vals MMLU-Pro 81.2% measured; GPQA 85.2% estimated ±1.6 pp.
- Conflicts: AA marks GLM-4.5 deprecated (superseded by GLM-4.6); official docs list GLM-4.5-Flash as active "Free" variant but no Flash-specific parameter count or benchmarks published; benchgap data is for GLM-4.5 family, not Flash-specific; official docs context 128K vs AA 130k (minor).

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- Tool use: **70/100.** Function calling, web search, tool streaming, context caching supported per official docs; deprecated status limits confidence.
- Reasoning: **65/100.** AA Intelligence Index 13 below class median (19); GPQA Diamond 79.9% estimated; deprecated by vendor/AA.
- Context window: **65/100.** 128K–130K tokens; below 256K+ of newer models.
- Multimodal: **15/100.** Text-only input/output per AA (template minimum for text-only).
- Coding: **72/100.** SWE-bench Verified 76.3% estimated; Vals LiveCodeBench 67.4% measured; positioned for coding & agents per official docs.
- Cost efficiency: **85/100.** Listed as free tier; MIT license open weights.
- **Overall Score: 68/100.** Half-up mean of the five non-cost dims; best-fit recommendation: free-tier agentic coding/Reasoning workloads; deprecated status means prefer GLM-4.6 or newer for new deployments.

